      <div><h4>How you shoot</h4><p>Hold it out like a Super 8 camera at chest or face height and watch the back. Your index finger pulls the trigger to record.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Good</h4><p>The most obvious way to use it, so it passes the hand-it-to-a-stranger test. No moving parts. The trigger REC is the classic Super 8 gesture.</p></div>
      <div><h4>Costs</h4><p>A 100 mm wide, boxy body: wider than the PXL-2000, closer to a 1980s camcorder. The screen faces the sky outdoors unless it's angled down slightly.</p></div>
      <div><h4>PCB</h4><p>One flat board along the bottom of the body. The screen connects at the rear, and the grip carries the battery and trigger on a short cable.</p></div>
